WEBVTT

00:00:00.850 --> 00:00:04.180
Playmaker, I'm serious.

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:08.150
You can't be indecisive.

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:12.360
Ai, do we really have to fight?

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:14.090
Stop being annoying!

00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:19.060
Fine.  I'll duel with all my strength!

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:21.030
That's the spirit.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:23.770
My turn!  I draw!

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:27.640
I activate the spell card, Cynet Closure!

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:32.080
I select a card from my deck 
and banish it facedown.

00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:36.350
Next, I summon Flame Bufferlo!

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:42.950
Due to the Continuous Spell, Cynet 
Optimization's effect, I summon Formud Skipper!

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:48.960
Link Summon!

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:53.330
Appear!  Link 2 Cyberse Witch!

00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:55.570
Cyberse Witch...

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:58.680
I'm curious what card he banished facedown.

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:02.310
But did he do it so he could 
use Cyberse Witch's effect?

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:05.540
Formud Skipper's effect 
activates from my graveyard!

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:10.280
I add a Level 5 or higher Cyberse 
from my deck to my hand!

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:13.490
I add Degrade Buster!

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:16.350
Flame Bufferlo's effect activates!

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:22.240
When it leaves the field, I discard 
Dotscaper from my hand to draw two cards!

00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:25.960
Dotscaper's effect activates 
from the graveyard!

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:28.400
It Special Summons itself!

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:33.610
Due to Cyberse Witch's effect, I banish 
Cynet Closure from my graveyard...

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:38.740
...to add Cyberse Magician and Cynet 
Ritual from my deck to my hand!

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:42.980
No matter what his true goal 
is, his moves are strong.

00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:44.950
I can't be careless.

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:52.000
I banish two Cyberses from my graveyard to 
Special Summon Degrade Buster from my hand!

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:55.860
I activate the Ritual Spell, Cynet Ritual!

00:01:56.130 --> 00:02:00.350
I tribute Degrade Buster to Ritual Summon!

00:02:00.830 --> 00:02:04.440
Appear, Cyberse Magician!

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:08.440
You brought out Cyberse Magician.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:12.540
But I don't think you're done yet.

00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:22.660
calling & feeling  I take your 
thoughts to heart  VRAINS

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:50.620
The data storm grazes my cheek, 
so I can't open my eyes

00:02:51.260 --> 00:03:00.570
What are we trying to find?  
Where are we trying to go?

00:03:01.130 --> 00:03:05.800
I won't make anyone sad anymore

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:14.350
I'll retrieve you  Let's go and look ahead

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:19.490
By meeting you, the world is in color

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:25.160
I'll protect you with an unseen bond

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:29.460
calling  With invisible wings

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:40.070
Destroy the dark and weakness within me

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:48.140
Cyberse Witch's effect activates!

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:52.940
I Special Summon a Level 4 or 
lower Cyberse from my graveyard!

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:57.150
The Special Summoned Clock 
Wyvern's effect activates!

00:03:57.150 --> 00:04:02.220
By halving its ATK, it Special 
Summons a Clock Token!

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:07.460
Sea Archiver's effect 
activates from my graveyard!

00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:13.500
When a monster is Special Summoned next to a 
Link Monster's link, it Special Summons itself!

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:15.230
Link Summon!

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:19.000
Appear, Link 2 Clock Spartoi!

00:04:19.970 --> 00:04:22.440
Clock Spartoi's effect activates!

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:25.910
I add Cynet Fusion from my deck to my hand!

00:04:27.510 --> 00:04:29.250
Link Summon!

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:33.850
Appear, Link 3 Transcode Talker!

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:38.420
I'm happy that you're not letting up!

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:41.490
That's the spirit, Playmaker!

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:43.500
Transcode's effect!

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:46.770
Transcode and the monster it's 
co-linked with gain 500 ATK

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:50.370
and can't be targeted by your effects!

00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:53.100
Clock Spartoi's effect activates!

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:59.000
I Special Summon a Level 4 or lower Cyberse 
from my graveyard by negating its effects.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:01.450
Resurrect, Clock Wyvern!

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:07.320
Transcode's effect activates!

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:13.540
I Special Summon a Level 3 or lower Cyberse 
Link Monster from my graveyard next to its link!

00:05:13.930 --> 00:05:16.830
Resurrect, Decode Talker!

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:22.170
I activate the spell, Cynet Fusion!

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:24.170
Fusion Summon!

00:05:25.940 --> 00:05:30.340
Appear!  Cyberse Clock Dragon!

00:05:35.750 --> 00:05:38.620
Cyberse Clock Dragon's effect activates!

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:41.090
I send five cards in my deck to my graveyard.

00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:45.280
Cyberse Clock Dragon gains 5000 ATK!

00:05:45.790 --> 00:05:47.960
7500 ATK?

00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:49.960
Here I go!  Battle!

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:54.730
Cyberse Clock Dragon attacks Fire Phoenix!

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:59.340
I can't believe you raised its ATK that high.

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:01.440
But that's good for me!

00:06:02.140 --> 00:06:04.880
I activate the trap, A.I.'s Show

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:10.100
I Special Summon Cyberses from 
my Extra Deck next to my links...

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:13.850
...whose total ATK are equal 
or less than Clock Dragon's.

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:15.800
And end the battle!

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:16.790
What?

00:06:16.790 --> 00:06:18.260
Come on out!

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:29.700
Since you raised its ATK, I 
was able to call out three.

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:32.440
But I knew you were going to do that.

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:36.420
I know everything about how you duel.

00:06:37.970 --> 00:06:39.810
I end my turn.

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:43.280
Now I'm much closer to victory.

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:46.750
Ai's army will soon be born.

00:06:46.750 --> 00:06:52.090
Ai, will making lots of copies satisfy you?

00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:54.130
Yeah.

00:06:54.130 --> 00:07:01.230
As you know, I got rid of 
my friends and became alone.

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:05.280
There were only six of us.

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:09.470
But we foolishly hated each other.

00:07:09.470 --> 00:07:12.440
Ai, that's not your fault!

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:17.180
I know.  But it doesn't 
matter whose fault it was.

00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:22.950
I'm like Earth's last surviving human.

00:07:22.950 --> 00:07:25.400
And that fact won't change.

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:30.530
Playmaker, I sort of understand how you felt.

00:07:30.740 --> 00:07:34.270
Being alone is very painful.

00:07:34.770 --> 00:07:36.030
Ai...

00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:39.240
Revolver may have been right.

00:07:39.240 --> 00:07:44.340
If this was the result, we shouldn't 
have been given free will.

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:48.180
Then I wouldn't have to suffer.

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:50.450
I understand your sadness.

00:07:50.450 --> 00:07:53.220
But don't let this fate sweep you away!

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:56.790
My fate...

00:07:57.260 --> 00:08:00.140
That depends on the result of this duel.

00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:02.930
That will determine my fate.

00:08:02.930 --> 00:08:05.660
Whether copies will be created or not.

00:08:05.660 --> 00:08:10.400
Even if you make copies, 
they won't be real friends.

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:13.400
Your loneliness won't go away!

00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:16.370
I never expected them to become my friends.

00:08:17.610 --> 00:08:20.380
Oh, I didn't tell you.

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:22.700
When my copies are created...

00:08:22.700 --> 00:08:27.950
...as the final activation trigger, my free 
will will be divided and given to them.

00:08:27.950 --> 00:08:29.920
What will happen to you?

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:32.800
My free will will be broken apart.

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:34.890
I'll be no more.

00:08:36.060 --> 00:08:40.900
If you win, you'll retrieve everything 
I took, and I'll be no more.

00:08:41.720 --> 00:08:46.740
But if I win, you'll be no more, 
and my copies will be created.

00:08:46.740 --> 00:08:50.210
Either way, I'll be no more.

00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:55.580
Ai, you're making me choose how you die?

00:08:55.850 --> 00:08:59.580
I know it's a bother, but that's right.

00:08:59.580 --> 00:09:03.960
I want to be with you at the end.

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:06.960
Ai, stop this nonsense!

00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:09.690
There still must be a way to save you!

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:12.630
You don't need to save me.

00:09:12.630 --> 00:09:17.640
Either way, you have to 
get back what I stole.

00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:20.540
So let's duel for real.

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:25.010
That's what Ai - your former partner - wants.

00:09:25.450 --> 00:09:26.540
Ai...

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:28.860
Here I go!

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:31.350
My turn!  I draw!

00:09:31.350 --> 00:09:36.830
He has Clock Dragon and Cyberse 
Magician on his field.

00:09:36.830 --> 00:09:39.020
As long as there's a Link Monster,

00:09:39.020 --> 00:09:42.670
they stop other monsters from being 
attacked or targeted by effects.

00:09:43.090 --> 00:09:49.810
So if they're both around, that means I 
can't attack, and my card effects are limited.

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:51.100
However...

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:55.040
I activate the spell card, A.I. Contact!

00:09:55.040 --> 00:10:01.380
I return the second Ignister A.I.Land in 
my hand to my deck to draw three cards.

00:10:01.710 --> 00:10:03.620
I got a good card.

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:06.220
I activate Wind Pegasus's effect!

00:10:06.220 --> 00:10:11.460
I destroy your spells and traps, up to 
the number of @Ignisters on the field!

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:16.460
I destroy Code Hack and Cynet Optimization!

00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:20.320
And I summon Hiyari.

00:10:21.570 --> 00:10:23.370
Hiyari's effect activates!

00:10:23.370 --> 00:10:29.570
I tribute a different @Ignister to add 
A.I.'s Ritual from my deck to my hand!

00:10:30.040 --> 00:10:33.710
If I tribute a Link Monster 
to activate this effect...

00:10:33.710 --> 00:10:39.220
...this card's Level increases for each of 
its Link Markers until the end of the turn!

00:10:39.550 --> 00:10:43.290
Then I add a Ritual Monster 
from my deck to my hand.

00:10:43.290 --> 00:10:46.620
I activate the Ritual Spell, A.I.'s Ritual!

00:10:47.990 --> 00:10:51.460
When there's a Water 
@Ignister on the field...

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:55.230
...I can banish an @Ignister from 
the graveyard instead of tributing.

00:10:55.230 --> 00:11:03.380
I tirbute Level 4 Hiyari and banish Level 4 
Pikari from my graveyard to Ritual Summon!

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:06.400
The water god dragon that hides in the ocean!

00:11:06.400 --> 00:11:11.350
Level 7 Water Leviathan @Ignister!

00:11:19.020 --> 00:11:21.760
Water Leviathan's effect activates!

00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:23.620
When it's Ritual Summoned...

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:29.800
...all your monsters whose original ATK are 
2300 or less are returned to your hand!

00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:33.740
Transcode returns to your Extra Deck!

00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:37.980
Now your Link Monster is gone!

00:11:37.980 --> 00:11:41.950
Clock Dragon and Cyberse Magician 
can't lock me down anymore.

00:11:42.910 --> 00:11:46.120
But Cyberse Magician is still in the way.

00:11:46.120 --> 00:11:51.320
As long as it's around, 
all damage is cut in half.

00:11:51.320 --> 00:11:53.930
So let's battle, Playmaker!

00:11:53.930 --> 00:11:57.530
Water Leviathan attacks Cyberse Magician!

00:11:57.530 --> 00:11:59.560
Water Leviathan's effect!

00:11:59.560 --> 00:12:03.130
Your battling monster's ATK is halved!

00:12:04.440 --> 00:12:06.850
Cyberse Magician's effect!

00:12:06.850 --> 00:12:08.510
Damage is halved!

00:12:08.510 --> 00:12:10.980
But it'll still be destroyed!

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:16.450
Light Dragon's effect activates!

00:12:16.780 --> 00:12:21.540
When a different @Ignister 
deals you battle damage...

00:12:21.540 --> 00:12:24.390
...I Special Summon an 
@Ignister from my graveyard!

00:12:24.390 --> 00:12:26.790
Resurrect, Fire Phoenix!

00:12:29.730 --> 00:12:31.400
Fire Phoenix!

00:12:31.660 --> 00:12:36.100
Here comes my special double strike!

00:12:36.340 --> 00:12:39.800
Fire Phoenix attacks Clock Dragon!

00:12:39.800 --> 00:12:41.210
This attack is...

00:12:41.210 --> 00:12:44.780
Exactly!  You know what'll happen, Playmaker!

00:12:45.100 --> 00:12:51.020
Due to Judgment Arrows, Fire 
Phoenix's ATK are doubled to 4600!

00:12:51.300 --> 00:12:58.390
And when Fire Phoenix battles, its effect 
deals you damage equal to its ATK!

00:12:58.490 --> 00:13:05.500
So you'll take 4600 damage, 
and I win this duel!

00:13:05.500 --> 00:13:07.400
I won't let you!

00:13:07.400 --> 00:13:10.600
I activate Overfloater's 
effect from my graveyard!

00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:16.070
When you have more monsters than me, by 
banishing this card from my graveyard...

00:13:16.070 --> 00:13:20.350
...your monsters with equal or less ATK 
than the attacking monster's original ATK

00:13:20.350 --> 00:13:22.090
have their effects negated!

00:13:22.090 --> 00:13:23.410
What?

00:13:23.410 --> 00:13:26.880
Now all your monsters' effects are negated!

00:13:26.880 --> 00:13:31.160
Fire Phoenix's damage-dealing 
effect is also negated!

00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:42.270
Not bad.

00:13:42.270 --> 00:13:44.250
Actually, impressive.

00:13:44.250 --> 00:13:47.870
You sent that card to the 
graveyard without me noticing.

00:13:48.110 --> 00:13:51.610
I guess I'll have to use my special move.

00:13:51.610 --> 00:13:52.840
What?

00:13:52.840 --> 00:13:56.580
Ai's special move is... fighting spirit!

00:13:58.260 --> 00:14:00.050
Seriously.

00:14:00.050 --> 00:14:03.790
I activate the spell 
card, FA.I.ghting Spirit!

00:14:03.790 --> 00:14:08.530
I Special Summon an @Ignister from 
my graveyard by negating its effects.

00:14:08.530 --> 00:14:11.430
Resurrect, Fire Phoenix!

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:23.720
Everyone...

00:14:23.720 --> 00:14:26.340
This is my perfect field.

00:14:26.340 --> 00:14:30.380
This time, we'll truly become one.

00:14:32.750 --> 00:14:36.390
Appear!  The circuit that guides the dark!

00:14:37.360 --> 00:14:40.260
The summoning conditions 
are at least two monsters

00:14:40.260 --> 00:14:43.460
with 1500 or more ATK that 
have different Attributes!

00:14:43.460 --> 00:14:46.800
I use Fire Attribute Fire Phoenix...

00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:49.300
Water Attribute Water Leviathan...

00:14:49.300 --> 00:14:51.770
Earth Attribute Earth Golem...

00:14:51.770 --> 00:14:54.240
Wind Attribute Wind Pegasus...

00:14:54.240 --> 00:14:56.710
Light Attribute Light Dragon...

00:14:56.710 --> 00:14:59.440
And Dark Attribute Dark Templar!

00:14:59.440 --> 00:15:04.180
I set the six @Ignisters in the Link Markers!

00:15:07.150 --> 00:15:08.890
Link Summon!

00:15:08.890 --> 00:15:12.490
The six shine and become one!

00:15:12.740 --> 00:15:18.830
Superior!  Splendid!  
Stunning!  Elegant!  Super!

00:15:20.260 --> 00:15:23.940
One two three four...  I'm one short.

00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:27.170
Umm...  Ultra super!

00:15:27.170 --> 00:15:28.770
That's six!

00:15:28.770 --> 00:15:29.570
Watch this!

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:35.350
I've enhanced Bohman's program 
to create my ultimate move!

00:15:35.350 --> 00:15:38.650
Appear, Link 6!

00:15:39.220 --> 00:15:43.850
The Arrival Cyberse @Ignister!

00:15:46.220 --> 00:15:47.990
Link 6!

00:15:47.990 --> 00:15:54.510
The Arrival has 1000 ATK for every 
monster used to Link Summon it.

00:15:54.510 --> 00:15:57.010
Six monsters were used!

00:15:57.010 --> 00:16:00.740
Therefore, The Arrival has 6000 ATK!

00:16:00.740 --> 00:16:06.840
And this card gains 1000 ATK 
for every card on my field.

00:16:06.840 --> 00:16:09.810
There are four cards on my field.

00:16:09.810 --> 00:16:12.920
So it gains 4000 ATK.

00:16:12.920 --> 00:16:18.320
And once per turn, I place 
a counter on this card.

00:16:18.320 --> 00:16:20.930
10000 ATK?

00:16:20.930 --> 00:16:23.160
It still has another effect!

00:16:23.480 --> 00:16:27.460
Once per turn, The Arrival 
can destroy a monster.

00:16:27.460 --> 00:16:33.120
Afterwards, I Special Summon an @Ignister 
Token next to this card's link.

00:16:33.120 --> 00:16:34.010
What?

00:16:35.770 --> 00:16:37.510
How disappointing.

00:16:37.510 --> 00:16:40.980
Bye bye, Cyberse Clock Dragon.

00:16:46.150 --> 00:16:53.040
Since I gained another card on my 
field, The Arrival's ATK increases!

00:16:53.760 --> 00:16:57.360
But Clock Dragon's effect activates!

00:16:57.620 --> 00:17:03.930
When your effect sends it to the graveyard, 
I add a spell card in my deck to my hand.

00:17:04.180 --> 00:17:05.670
I'm not done!

00:17:07.440 --> 00:17:08.910
Link Summon!

00:17:08.910 --> 00:17:13.480
Appear, Link 1 Darkwight @Ignister!

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:16.980
0 ATK?

00:17:16.980 --> 00:17:21.590
When Darkwight is linked, it 
can't be the attack target.

00:17:21.590 --> 00:17:26.720
So to defeat me, you have 
to defeat The Arrival.

00:17:26.720 --> 00:17:29.310
I end my turn.

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:31.130
Now bring it on!

00:17:31.130 --> 00:17:35.670
If you don't, your monsters 
will keep being destroyed!

00:17:36.090 --> 00:17:39.640
My turn!  I draw!

00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:45.110
With 11000 ATK, I'll have 
to deal with it first.

00:17:45.110 --> 00:17:47.850
I summon Cyberse Gadget!

00:17:49.350 --> 00:17:54.990
It Special Summons a Level 2 or lower 
monster from my graveyard by negating its effects!

00:17:54.990 --> 00:17:57.960
Resurrect, Formud Skipper!

00:17:58.960 --> 00:18:00.490
Link Summon!

00:18:01.460 --> 00:18:05.430
Appear, Link 2 Cyberse Wicckid!

00:18:05.430 --> 00:18:09.300
Formud Skipper's effect 
activates from the graveyard!

00:18:09.300 --> 00:18:14.110
I add a Level 5 or higher Cyberse 
from my deck to my hand!

00:18:14.110 --> 00:18:17.680
Then Cyberse Gadget's effect activates!

00:18:17.680 --> 00:18:22.210
When it's sent to the graveyard, 
I Special Summon a Gadget Token.

00:18:22.210 --> 00:18:24.550
Cyberse Wicckid's effect!

00:18:24.550 --> 00:18:27.690
Since a monster was Special 
Summoned next to its link...

00:18:27.690 --> 00:18:33.690
...I banish Dotscaper from my graveyard to 
add Cyberse Synchron from my deck to my hand!

00:18:33.690 --> 00:18:36.390
Then Dotscaper's effect activates!

00:18:36.390 --> 00:18:39.830
When it's banished, I can Special Summon it!

00:18:40.910 --> 00:18:42.230
Link Summon!

00:18:42.770 --> 00:18:47.200
Appear, Link 2 Exslayer!

00:18:50.910 --> 00:18:54.010
Parallel eXceed's effect 
activates from my hand!

00:18:54.010 --> 00:19:00.950
When I successfully Link Summon, I Special 
Summon this card from my hand next to its link!

00:19:01.240 --> 00:19:04.920
Then I Special Summon a 
second Parallel eXceed!

00:19:05.920 --> 00:19:11.200
When it's Special Summoned due to its own 
effect, its Level and DEF are halved.

00:19:12.200 --> 00:19:19.700
With these two Level 4 Parallel 
eXceeds, I build the Overlay Network!

00:19:26.980 --> 00:19:29.110
Xyz Summon!

00:19:29.960 --> 00:19:35.620
Rank 4 Firewall eXceed Dragon!

00:19:37.920 --> 00:19:40.160
eXceed Dragon's effect!

00:19:40.160 --> 00:19:47.770
For every Link Marker that a Link Monster 
linked to this card has, it gains 500 ATK!

00:19:47.770 --> 00:19:50.370
Exslayer's effect activates!

00:19:50.370 --> 00:19:54.120
When I Xyz Summon next to its link...

00:19:54.120 --> 00:19:59.980
...I tribute a monster to Special Summon 
a Level 4 or lower monster from my hand!

00:19:59.980 --> 00:20:05.420
I tribute Gadget Token to 
Special Summon Widget Kid!

00:20:05.420 --> 00:20:10.990
I see.  You Xyz Summoned 
to bring out Widget Kid.

00:20:10.990 --> 00:20:12.890
So your plan is to...

00:20:12.890 --> 00:20:15.360
Widget Kid's effect activates!

00:20:15.360 --> 00:20:18.960
I Special Summon a Cyberse from my hand!

00:20:18.960 --> 00:20:21.830
Appear, Cyberse Synchron!

00:20:21.830 --> 00:20:24.530
Cyberse Synchron's effect activates!

00:20:25.440 --> 00:20:32.140
A Level 4 or lower monster's Level increases 
by its original Level until the end of the turn!

00:20:32.140 --> 00:20:38.170
Level 1 Cyberse Synchron 
tunes Level 6 Widget Kid!

00:20:41.890 --> 00:20:46.090
6 + 1 = ......8!

00:20:46.090 --> 00:20:48.080
Synchro Summon!

00:20:48.080 --> 00:20:54.330
Appear, Level 7 Cyberse Quantum Dragon!

00:20:57.330 --> 00:20:58.910
You didn't fall for my trick!

00:20:58.910 --> 00:21:01.960
I expected you'd bring out Quantum.

00:21:01.960 --> 00:21:07.110
Because you have to use Quantum's effect 
to do something about The Arrival.

00:21:07.110 --> 00:21:11.980
Battle!  Quantum Dragon attacks The Arrival!

00:21:14.450 --> 00:21:17.450
Quantum Dragon's effect activates!

00:21:17.450 --> 00:21:19.820
I return your monster to your hand!

00:21:19.820 --> 00:21:24.300
When this effect activates, 
I can attack again!

00:21:24.300 --> 00:21:27.060
I'm happy you're fighting me seriously!

00:21:27.060 --> 00:21:29.740
But you're not serious enough.

00:21:29.740 --> 00:21:32.600
I knew you'd try this from the start!

00:21:32.600 --> 00:21:34.770
The Arrival's effect!

00:21:35.910 --> 00:21:40.540
When there's a counter on this card, 
other cards' effects can't affect it!

00:21:41.550 --> 00:21:44.880
The Arrival doesn't return to my hand!

00:21:44.880 --> 00:21:48.050
Too bad.  It's striking back, Playmaker!

00:21:48.050 --> 00:21:49.890
The attack won't stop!

00:21:56.830 --> 00:21:58.800
I now win!

00:22:05.550 --> 00:22:09.520
I was told repeatedly

00:22:09.520 --> 00:22:16.970
Only tales of dreams

00:22:17.320 --> 00:22:23.960
Is my life precious?

00:22:24.200 --> 00:22:26.930
Make up for  Make up for

00:22:27.300 --> 00:22:34.440
The next sentimental

00:22:39.280 --> 00:22:45.700
I'm not a machine

00:22:48.420 --> 00:22:52.140
I cry a single tear

00:22:53.630 --> 00:22:57.360
A single answer moves me

00:22:58.530 --> 00:23:07.720
We helplessly sing for someone we can't reach

00:23:08.340 --> 00:23:13.150
Are you ready?

00:23:13.650 --> 00:23:18.500
Oh oh oh

00:23:19.020 --> 00:23:23.720
Are you ready?

00:23:24.320 --> 00:23:30.810
Are you ready?

00:23:37.840 --> 00:23:41.000
An AI with versatile free will has a flaw:

00:23:41.000 --> 00:23:45.340
It's become more human-like than humans.

00:23:45.340 --> 00:23:51.210
Since Ai has superior intelligence, he 
struggles with the framework he created.

00:23:51.210 --> 00:23:56.610
Sensing the change in his partner's 
heart, what can Playmaker do?

00:23:56.610 --> 00:23:59.320
Find a way to backtrack, Ai!

00:23:59.970 --> 00:24:03.970
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:
Self Breakdown

00:24:03.970 --> 00:24:06.090
Into the VRAINS!
